I left out both operations additions. The node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem authority, and calling `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. Neither is granted, and sending the input's text to an outside service would also leak it. If you want them, the graph's `with` clause has to be changed first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{conversation-context, response-result};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/tool-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(ctx: conversation-context) -> response-result;
}
```

